      "reviewer": "Claude Opus 5.5",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-09-28T17:38:45Z",
      "note": "Loss. eth_getLogs Transfer from Votemarket 0x8c2c5a295450ddff4cb360ca73fccc12243d14d9 on Arbitrum, blocks 440837126..440900000, and on Base, blocks 43242900..43243100: 50 Arbitrum transactions (source-4, blocks 440842446..440843755) and 4 Base transactions (source-5, block 43242971) each pay one campaign to the attacker 0x595b8888858e2748da23eb026cac06ef1bf9d497 and a fee share to 0x175e94ad5029e62ef876d94eb15f822c8027e4c0 (protocol fee, not counted). Arbitrum payouts are LaPoste wrapped tokens (pWFRAX, pDOLA, ppmUSD, pSPELL, pGHO, pCVX, pASF, popASF, pMUSD, pOUSD, psdUSD, pUSDC) backed by escrow on Ethereum; the attacker bridged them back, and Ethereum Transfer logs to the attacker in blocks 24638218..24638252 (CCIP manual executions 0x73f79b8ad0d48a8884ad3a8aa91d23ed2e27909cf7fee8e129ce0e62b3289695 .. 0x1bdd155927dae9b30caa72faa09c6116e9c214650b5ffc34ef52922a2b88fb1f) release exactly the claimed quantities of the underlying from LaPoste escrow 0x96006425da428e45c282008b00004a00002b345e, so components are recorded as the Ethereum underlying. Base payouts: USDC 7169.611786, USDp 959.999999999998732685, CRV 30959.999999999995847609. Excluded: 57596.332162042591730353 opASF (no price series) and a 5828.178491 transfer of token 0x5eb3059e5deb2625967e0010a01ab0bbe07186cc (named USDC, unpriced) from escrow 0x9600c981f6f2d1bbc19cec22b3d73200002b345e that duplicates the pUSDC amount. sdUSD is taken at par. Prices are DefiLlama samples at or before the last claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "source-19",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "Claude Opus 5.5",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-09-28T17:38:45Z",
      "note": "Root cause, anchor and age. Verified L1BlockOracleUpdater (Etherscan V2 getsourcecode, 0xae74643a...): receiveMessage(chainId, sender, data) is onlyLaPoste and reverts only if chainId != 1 && sender != L1_SENDER && sender != address(this), so any sender on chain 1 passes; it then writes the block into every configured oracle. debug_traceTransaction(callTracer) of source-1 (block 440837126, index 1): the CCIP transmit reaches LaPoste 0xf0000058000021003e4754dca700c766de7601c2, which calls the updater; the updater calls insertBlockNumber (0x5478dad4) on six oracles including 0x36f5b50d70df3d3e1c7e1baf06c32119408ef7d8, and emits the block at log 0 (number 99999999, epoch 1773273600). LaPoste log 1 carries source chain 1, receiver 0xae74643a... and sender 0x595b8888858e2748da23eb026cac06ef1bf9d497, versus L1_SENDER() = 0x59b66e337c5a2c6229c058e69d06e967ac4d3956; the originating Ethereum message is 0xeab3c9790e9eedc437d7209f185dc901d8ebddbaeefeeb2a4aa0ec70791365b8. Earliest exercise: every LaPoste message-received log (topic 0xe12070ab31c354e32f755984628cc3af260121ee9015cf34637b824e34d00bc7) for this receiver from its deployment to block 440900000 has sender 0xae74643a... (51 logs) except source-1. The Base leg ran 5 minutes later through the single-oracle updater 0xb104d3a146f909d9d722005a5bdb17e570c88c6a with the same check, and its loss is merged. Age: eth_getCode of the updater is empty at block 317381732 and keccak256 of its runtime is the recorded hash at blocks 317381733 and 440837125; source-2 creates it via CreateX 0xba5ed099633d3b313e4d5f7bdc1305d3c28ba5ed and CREATE3 proxy 0x1a5f182c21b920a5323168e25153122d6ae7c83a; it has no upgrade path. The oracle accepts its writes only after governance Safe 0xb0552b6860ce5c0202976db056b5e3cc4f9cc765 execTransaction source-3 (block 317409092, 1 hour 54 minutes after deployment): authorizedBlockNumberProviders(updater) is false at block 317409091 and true at 317409092 and through the exploit. That authorization is necessary to the poisoned oracle state and is the latest reset."
